# Credentials for the MCP servers. Copy to .env and fill in.
#
# An MCP client passes a server only a short allow-list of environment
# variables (PATH, APPDATA, TEMP...), so a client-launched server cannot see
# your shell. tools/ipcc_mcp.py reads this file at startup to stay
# self-sufficient. Anything the client does pass takes precedence.

# Either the Vertex AI route (uses Application Default Credentials on disk):
GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI=true
GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=your-gcp-project
GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=global

# ...or a single AI Studio key instead of the three above:
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Shared cache (Cache v2, tools/cache_backend.py). OPTIONAL: with both unset
# the cache falls back to local disk, which is what local dev, CI and the tests
# use. Set both to share one cache across Cloud Run replicas and across
# redeploys, so a cold container skips the ~42 s ERA5 fetch + 12.9 s GEV fit.
# Values come from the Upstash console (REST tab); the token is a secret.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-db.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Where the disk tier writes when Redis is not configured (default shown).
# CRG_CACHE_DIR=data/cache/kv

# Precomputed cache entries shipped with the code (ERA5 fits, IPCC grounding),
# read before Redis or disk. Defaults to tools/cache_seed/; an empty value
# turns them off (scripts/precompute_grounding.py does that, to compute instead of read).
# CRG_CACHE_SEED_DIR=

# Spend guard (rag/spend_guard.py). The defaults below apply when a line is left
# unset; each takes a number, or "off". DEPLOY.md ("Spend guard") has the cost
# arithmetic behind them.
#
# Daily budget for model calls, in US dollars per UTC day. Each call reserves
# its worst case before it is sent and is charged what it was billed after.
# Shared by every instance when both UPSTASH_ values above are set; otherwise
# each process (each Cloud Run instance) has a budget of its own.
# CRG_DAILY_MODEL_BUDGET_USD=0.15
#
# UI: reports that need new model calls, per browser session. Later reports
# still run, with model calls paused; cached answers keep their citations.
# CRG_SESSION_FRESH_REPORTS=5
#
# API: requests per client per window on /report, /query and /triage.
# CRG_API_RATE_LIMIT=10
# CRG_API_RATE_WINDOW_S=60

# GEV bootstrap refits per hazard fit (default 300 stationary / 200 trend-adjusted).
# Read at import and part of the fit-cache key, so changing it refits rather than
# reusing. 150 is the measured floor that still preserves the tail CI.
# CRG_BOOTSTRAP_N=150

# TypeSafe Jev (adr/0002). OPTIONAL and off by default: off | triage | verify | all.
# With it on, some user questions (triage) or IPCC statements (verify) are sent to
# a US provider; read LIMITATIONS.md ("Jev") first. JEV_BASE_URL picks one of two
# vetted providers: unset for TypeSafe direct, or https://api.experientiallabs.ai
# for the Experiential Labs gateway. The key (for that provider) is a secret.
# CRG_JEV=off
# JEV_BASE_URL=
# JEV_API_KEY=
